🛡️ OWASP ZAP – Web Vulnerability Scanning

Performed an automated web security assessment of the DVWA (Damn Vulnerable Web Application) using OWASP ZAP in a controlled local lab environment. 
🔍 The scan helped identify common web security issues, including missing anti-clickjacking headers, server version information disclosure, and missing X-Content-Type-Options headers. 
📊 I analyzed the detected alerts, reviewed their risk levels and confidence, and documented the findings along with recommended mitigation techniques.
🔐 This practical helped me understand automated vulnerability scanning, security headers, information disclosure, and the importance of strengthening web application security. 🚀
